    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0200" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg100"/>

                <head>No. 85.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Torreão de
                    Barros.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 20,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of Mr. Borges’ note of the 12th instant, expressing the hope that the subject of
                    the provision by United States law for punishing the crime of counterfeiting the
                    paper currency of foreign governments may be brought to the attention of
                    Congress at its next sesssion, and to say, in reply, that I shall have the honor
                    to again address the chairman of the Committee on the Judiciary with reference
                    to the matter.</p>
                <p>Accept sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
